Now let me assess the complete picture based on my independent verification.

**Verification summary:**
- All key papers verified: arXiv:2605.01647 ✓, arXiv:2604.08554 ✓, arXiv:2502.15654 ✓, Strong Model Collapse ICLR 2025 ✓
- Qwen3-0.6B confirmed on HuggingFace ✓; `enable_thinking=False` tokenizer hard switch confirmed ✓; GitHub discussion #1329 confirmed ✓
- No competing work found doing generational depth scoring (Gen0/Gen1/Gen2 ordinal labeling) — novelty confirmed
- New potentially uncited paper found: arXiv:2602.10531 "From Collapse to Improvement: Statistical Perspectives on the Evolutionary Dynamics of Iterative Training on Contaminated Sources" (Feb 2026)
- Round 6 issues: ✓ thinking mode hard switch + post-hoc scan properly addresses Issue 1; ✓ fixed-total-size conditions (200K per condition) properly addresses Issue 2

